      <data key="d0">function</data>
      <data key="d1">python</data>
      <data key="d3">_apply_smart_window_size</data>
      <data key="d5">['self']</data>
      <data key="d4">Size and center the window based on available screen geometry.

Detects the primary monitor's usable area (excluding taskbar) and
sizes the window slightly smaller with a small margin. Caps at
1400x900 on large screens and floors at 800x600 minimum. Falls
back to 1400x900 if screen detection fails.</data>
    </node>
